  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-17T08:02:14.465Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "1. Open VRChat in VR mode with a Valve Index\n\n2. While playing, physically disconnect the Index; this removes the audio device out for the headset\n\n3. VRChat's audio device list is gone, and nothing can be selected. Audio will not work until the game is restarted.\n\nWhat would be nice is if I could restart VRChat's audio engine, or refresh the list of available audio devices, after it gets corrupted.\n\nEven better would be if, when the selected audio device disappears, VRC could detect this and select a new audio device if possible.",
